WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.980
If glia feed axons, the fuel must leave the glial cell.

2
00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:09.400
What happens if you block the exit?

3
00:00:10.433 --> 00:00:12.613
Lactate leaves on transporters.

4
00:00:13.273 --> 00:00:19.073
In 2012, Jeffrey Rothstein's group showed that one, MCT1, is concentrated in

5
00:00:19.073 --> 00:00:20.153
oligodendrocytes.

6
00:00:20.967 --> 00:00:24.367
In spinal cord slices, they withheld glucose briefly.

7
00:00:25.347 --> 00:00:28.487
Some slices also got a drug that blocks MCT1.

8
00:00:29.367 --> 00:00:31.027
Some of those also got lactate.

9
00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:34.500
What happens to the motor neurons in each condition?

10
00:00:41.033 --> 00:00:43.133
With glucose withheld, they survived.

11
00:00:44.113 --> 00:00:45.413
Add the blocker, and they died.

12
00:00:46.313 --> 00:00:49.093
Add lactate with the blocker still on, and they survived.

13
00:00:52.583 --> 00:00:57.923
That is a rescue. The best reading is that the neurons lacked lactate, which glia

14
00:00:57.923 --> 00:00:58.923
are thought to supply.

15
00:00:59.823 --> 00:01:01.543
Other drug effects are not ruled out.

16
00:01:02.483 --> 00:01:08.683
In living mice, lowering MCT1 in the spinal cord made axons swell and degenerate.

17
00:01:09.383 --> 00:01:10.423
Motor neurons were lost.

18
00:01:11.433 --> 00:01:13.613
A cleaner test came in 2021.

19
00:01:14.713 --> 00:01:19.933
Deleting MCT1 only in oligodendrocyte lineage cells left young mice normal.

20
00:01:20.967 --> 00:01:24.847
As the mice aged, axons degenerated and myelin thinned.

21
00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:31.160
Side by side: with glial respiration switched off, adult brain axons were spared

22
00:01:31.160 --> 00:01:32.220
over the months studied.

23
00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:38.200
Remove MCT1, the proposed export route, and axons degenerate with age.

24
00:01:39.233 --> 00:01:44.293
One caution: the two sets of mice were not followed over matched ages, and myelin

25
00:01:44.293 --> 00:01:45.293
also thinned late.

26
00:01:46.267 --> 00:01:48.287
So the picture that fits is this.

27
00:01:49.167 --> 00:01:54.207
Oligodendrocytes run glycolysis and export lactate or pyruvate through MCT1.

28
00:01:55.047 --> 00:02:00.067
The axon turns any lactate back into pyruvate and burns it in its own mitochondria.

29
00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:05.980
Still unknown: the exact route, and how much of an axon's ATP this supplies.

30
00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:10.240
These experiments infer the transfer; none of them traces it.

31
00:02:13.033 --> 00:02:15.813
Astrocytes are a second, contested candidate.

32
00:02:16.693 --> 00:02:21.573
One sensor study in mouse cortex reported a lactate gradient from astrocytes to

33
00:02:21.573 --> 00:02:22.573
neurons.

34
00:02:23.017 --> 00:02:28.777
Another saw stimulated neurons raise their own glycolysis, with no sign of lactate

35
00:02:28.777 --> 00:02:29.777
import.

36
00:02:30.117 --> 00:02:34.157
So the astrocyte shuttle remains a hypothesis with partial support.

37
00:02:35.167 --> 00:02:38.807
For the axon under myelin, the evidence fits one picture.

38
00:02:39.707 --> 00:02:41.547
Whoever wraps the axon helps feed it.
